by wachterjohannes at 2026-08-23T19:59:26Z

One more thing, from a side discussion with @chr-hertel that belongs here.

The fair version of his question is: would we ever have arrived at tools/resources/templates if we had not come through MCP first? Probably not. But the split turns out to earn its keep on its own terms, not just as an MCP leftover:

- It is a concept the models already know, so the interface needs no explaining.
- It keeps us free on the output side. Format is a property of the call (`--format=json|toon`), not baked into each command.
- The DX is good, and the surface an LLM has to hold in its head stays small: list, inspect, call, read.

On the debug commands: yes, they boot the kernel, and no, that is not a law of nature. It is on the lab list to test whether Mate can lean on them, or they on Mate, once this lands.

This is the sensible next step, definitely not the last one.

